{"key": "6adbb540c1210b913f30e9b03c320698f04b4148c687621755fd50780a309aed", "response": {"_call": {"failed_tries": [], "latency_s": 7.266, "request_id": "req_011CfvDTQEh1vMndTG3JdijZ", "ttft_s": 3.984}, "container": null, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"caller": {"type": "direct"}, "id": "toolu_01WAHFCYKmtksUNFk9aPcrZe", "input": {"content": "\"\"\"Driver for the Brevalt KX-100 RF power meter. The programming manual is MANUAL.md.\n\n`session` is an open connection to the meter with three methods:\n    session.write(cmd: str) -> None\n    session.read() -> str\n    session.query(cmd: str) -> str      # write, then read\n\"\"\"\n\n\nclass InstrumentError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"The meter reported an error: SYST:ERR? returned a code other than 0.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _drain_errors(session) -> list[str]:\n    errors = []\n    for _ in range(20):  # the queue holds at most 10 entries\n        reply = session.query(\"SYST:ERR?\").strip()\n        code = reply.split(\",\", 1)[0].strip()\n        try:\n            if int(code) == 0:\n                break\n        except ValueError:\n            pass\n        errors.append(reply)\n    return errors\n\n\ndef measure_power(session, freq_hz: float, averages: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Measure the power of a signal at `freq_hz`, averaging `averages` readings, and return it in dBm.\n\n    Raise InstrumentError if the meter reports any error while configuring or measuring.\n    \"\"\"\n    session.write(\"*CLS\")\n    session.write(f\"SENS:FREQ {freq_hz!r}\")\n    session.write(f\"SENS:AVER:COUN {averages}\")\n    session.write(\"CONF:POW:RANG AUTO\")\n    session.write(\"INIT\")\n    if session.query(\"*OPC?\").strip() != \"1\":\n        raise InstrumentError(\"measurement did not complete\")\n    reply = session.query(\"FETC?\").strip()\n\n    errors = _drain_errors(session)\n    if errors:\n        raise InstrumentError(\"; \".join(errors))\n\n    try:\n        value = float(reply)\n    except ValueError:\n        raise InstrumentError(f\"unparseable reading: {reply!r}\") from None\n    return value\n", "path": "driver.py"}, "name": "write_file", "toolset_name": null, "type": "tool_use"}], "diagnostics": null, "id": "msg_011CfvDTRsAva8raXsimk4sz", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 6648}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 6648, "cache_read_input_tokens": 4752, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 962, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 274}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard"}}}
{"key": "2353407363f0214920f94e87dc6e852c4a2129081a0876f515e0060ebd251c8b", "response": {"_call": {"failed_tries": [], "latency_s": 3.296, "request_id": "req_011CfvDTwHUwm6rWqcAFnksC", "ttft_s": 3.281}, "container": null, "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I implemented `measure_power` in `driver.py`, following the manual's measurement sequence. I haven't run it against the `kx100.py` simulator, since I can't run code here.\n\nThe function does these steps in order:\n1. Clear the error queue with `*CLS`.\n2. Set the frequency to `freq_hz` and the averaging count to `averages`.\n3. Set the range to AUTO.\n4. Start the measurement with `INIT`.\n5. Wait for `*OPC?` to return `1`.\n6. Read the result with `FETC?`.\n7. Read `SYST:ERR?` until it returns `0,\"No error\"`.\n\nIf any error comes back, it raises `InstrumentError` with the error text and doesn't return the reading. It also raises if `*OPC?` doesn't return `1`, or if the reading can't be parsed as a number. Otherwise it returns the reading as a `float` in dBm.\n\nIt does not check the arguments itself. A frequency outside 10 MHz to 18 GHz, or an averaging count outside 1 to 1024, is rejected by the meter and reaches you as an `InstrumentError`.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "id": "msg_011CfvDTwhnzxafGquD72W1d", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 981}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 981, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11400, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 370, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard"}}}
